erged from a contested Republican primary and runoff, aided by Donald Trump's endorsement after Jackson Lahmeyer withdrew, while Democrat John Croisant enters the general election with far fewer resources. Every major rating outlet calls the district Safe, Solid, or Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Croisant roughly a two percent chance.\n\nThe financial picture is similarly one-sided: Tedford has raised about 2.4 million dollars to Croisant's roughly 200 thousand, with outside groups adding to the Republican advantage. No public general-election polling exists, so the outlook rests on district partisanship, expert ratings, and money. Croisant would need an unusually large national swing to make this race competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -11.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0097, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0191, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0497, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0244, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0398, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.05, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0401, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0392, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0141, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.021, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0259, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0198, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0096, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0036, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0029, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0175, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0049, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem"